%% 06_ARCHITECTURE.mmd — Hackathon multi-AI workflow: architecture diagram (SSOT for node IDs
%% per shared contract §4).
%% %%
%% WHAT THIS DIAGRAM SHOWS
%%   Two machines, three roles. S1 (research) decomposes an unknown topic into a frozen, versioned
%%   Mission Package and runs two concurrent modes: research (on demand) and observe (continuous,
%%   read-only, tier-2 degradable). S2 is the development fleet: five humans, five machines, one
%%   writer per workspace/branch/worktree, building against the frozen package through
%%   task-selected capability bundles. GitHub + CI is the single source of truth; human authority
%%   (package approval, merge, escalation) is never held by AI. Failure and degradation paths are
%%   drawn dashed red; read-only observation dashed grey; capability selection dotted purple;
%%   normal artifact handoff solid blue. Every arrow label is an artifact name or a named concrete
%%   event. The coordination/runtime boundary is existing tooling (Git + supervised agents) — no
%%   custom scheduler, no message bus. All examples in this package are synthetic.
%% %%
%% RENDER COMMAND (from repo root)
%%   npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i 06_ARCHITECTURE.mmd -o render/06_ARCHITECTURE.svg -w 2400
%%   npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli -i 06_ARCHITECTURE.mmd -o render/06_ARCHITECTURE.png -w 2400
%%   (renders committed at -w 2400; at -w 1600 the 16px type sits at the floor of legibility)
%% %%
%% VERSIONS ACTUALLY USED
%%   @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli 11.17.0 (npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli --version)
%%   mermaid 11.17.2 (bundled by mermaid-cli 11.17.0)
%% %%
%% FALLBACKS APPLIED
%%   1. AG edge collapse (contract §4, E19–E23): ten edges out of MP + AG into five lanes rendered
%%      as a hairball at 1600 px. Collapsed AG to ONE dotted edge into L1 labelled
%%      "per-task bundle — every lane, selected per task". Semantics unchanged: the bundle serves
%%      every lane, selected per task.
%%   2. E29 reroute (contract §4, collision clause): E29 (REPO --> L1) collided with E27 near the
%%      lane stack; rerouted to REPO --> L5 per the contract's named option, keeping the
%%      "(any lane)" wording. Semantics unchanged.
%%   No other fallbacks: RUNTIME nesting kept (renders cleanly), node IDs and edge semantics as
%%   specified in the contract inventory.
%% %%
%% KNOWN COSMETIC ARTIFACT
%%   ELK orders the five lane nodes visually as 2,5,3,4,1 (left to right). Lane identity is
%%   self-describing in each node label (human N, machine N, workstream-N), so the ordering
%%   carries no semantics and is not corrected by fighting the layout engine.
%% %%
%% LAYOUT ADJUSTMENTS (syntax/layout only, semantics untouched)
%%   - ELK direction DOWN (contract init block says RIGHT): at 1600 px raster width the LR layout
%%     scaled 14 px type to ~5.5 px and was illegible; the TD orientation keeps the aspect near
%%     square so 16 px type renders at ~8.6 px at 1600 px width.
%%   - Long node and edge labels wrapped with <br/> at word boundaries; label text is verbatim
%%     from the contract inventory.
%%   - One invisible layout link (CI ~~~ LEG1) places the legend below the diagram body instead
%%     of beside it.
%%   - The contract's elk.spacing.* keys are kept in the init block but verified inert in
%%     mermaid 11.17.2: three spacing configurations (32/60/12/8, 40/64/16/10, 24/48/8/6)
%%     produced byte-identical viewBox geometry, so ELK layout here runs on its defaults.

